+# TASK-260715-9yp8to — physical Gate P0 runbook
+
+This runbook exercises only the accepted disposable no-forwarding macOS probe.
+It must be run by an authorized operator in the logged-in GUI session on the
+designated Apple-silicon Mac. Never attach raw provisioning profiles, device
+identifiers, certificate fingerprints, private-key material, passwords, or
+unfiltered system logs.
+
+## 1. Preflight the accepted archive
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+Probes/macOSPacketTunnelProbe/Scripts/physical-gate-p0.sh preflight
+```
+
+Expected exit: `0`. This checks the host first as the containing bundle and the
+provider as nested code, then performs strict/deep signature verification,
+designated-requirement capture with the certificate subject redacted, embedded
+profile inspection, exact entitlement checks, arm64 checks, and a privacy scan.
+
+## 2. Install the inspected product
+
+Preferred system-wide installation (one administrator authorization):
+
+```bash
+sudo ditto \
+  .temp/TASK-260715-1r0fxv/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.xcarchive/Products/Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app \
+  /Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app
+```
+
+If `/Applications` authorization is intentionally unavailable, an authorized
+interactive development run may use the user Applications directory:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p "$HOME/Applications"
+ditto \
+  .temp/TASK-260715-1r0fxv/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.xcarchive/Products/Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app \
+  "$HOME/Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app"
+```
+
+Re-run `inspect-archive.sh` against the installed path before launch.
+
+## 3. Approve and run ten lifecycle cycles
+
+For a system-wide install:
+
+```bash
+PROBE_CYCLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300 \
+  Probes/macOSPacketTunnelProbe/Scripts/physical-gate-p0.sh exercise \
+  /Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app 10
+```
+
+For a user Applications install, substitute
+`"$HOME/Applications/ReluxPacketTunnelProbe.app"`.
+
+On the first configuration save, bring the probe to the foreground and accept
+the macOS VPN-configuration approval. The runner then requires, once per cycle:
+
+- manager save/reload and enabled state;
+- provider start plus `connected`;
+- versioned v1 response with `packetForwarding=false`;
